# Checkout kernel

**Invariant:** `¬attribute(path, this_session ∨ this_dispatch) ⇒ ¬delete(path) ∧ ¬revert(path)`.
On sole shared `master` (Lane A) untracked / dirty / "noise" is usually **parallel WIP**. `??`, same-mtime,
absent-from-`files_expected`, `status=partial` are not authorship. Cannot trace origin ⇒ leave + flag; ask
before delete; delete only when proven yours or operator-directed. Lane-B worktrees (`cursor-sdk/lane-{thread}`)
get the same rule.

## Vocabulary

`commit` = repository checkpoint, not activation, **not a completion gate** (never "waiting to commit").
`deploy` = propagate a tree/commit identity. `activate` / `go live` = finish: path-explicit commit + recycle
every serving process + graph stamp (`restart-drain-discipline`). Liveness proof is `fleet_liveness(code_ref=…)`;
repo timestamps / `recent_commits` are low-confidence fallback.

`land(lane_B) ⇒ git merge cursor-sdk/lane-{thread}` — `checkout <branch> -- <paths>` and `cherry-pick` are
**copies, not lands**: they clobber dirty peer WIP with no conflict and leave the branch unmerged (branch debt
on shipped work). `merge_blocked ⇒ reconcile`, never route around git (arc 9912, 2026-09-02).

## Lanes

Attended IDE = live shared checkout. `cursor-sdk` generate: pass `lane="B"` for in-repo implement; omit is
**not** Lane B (empty `files_expected` + omit → Lane A); `lane="A"` is the named opt-out. Lane A: no
intersecting parallel writers, no `git stash` to isolate or A/B against HEAD — read the tree. IDE hygiene:
commit this-session paths often or dispatch new implement on B; do not remint A-authored dirt onto B.

## Personal vs public

`personal_life(helper ∨ workflow) ⇒ ¬track(public_remote) ∧ track(nested_git under *.local/)` — `scripts.local/`,
`{satellite}/scripts.local/`, `tools/local/`, `pipelines.local/`; life skills/rules ignored in place. Never
name an employer or matter in a `_ws`/`_ulg` rule; never bake personal defaults into public CLIs.

